			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement output channel management handlers\n\nIntroduce the complete set of RPC handlers in `CocoonService` for the `Vine` protocol to bridge the extension host with the Sky UI for output channel operations. This adds handlers for `CreateOutputChannel`, `AppendOutput`, `ClearOutput`, `DisposeOutput`, and `ShowOutput`.\n\nThe implementation emits Tauri events (`sky://output/*`) to the frontend, passing channel identifiers and payload data as JSON. `CreateOutputChannel` returns the assigned channel ID, while other operations trigger state updates or visibility toggles in the Sky workbench. These handlers complete the output panel IPC contract, enabling extensions to manage logging channels and display terminal-like output asynchronously.",
			"SHA": "4fef1677bec1ca93773b4a867f591969043e4b67"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:33:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1072,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement command registration and execution handlers\n\nIntroduce three new RPC handlers in `CocoonService` to complete the command lifecycle contract defined in the `Vine` protocol: `RegisterCommand`, `UnregisterCommand`, and `ExecuteContributedCommand`.\n\nThe implementation bridges the extension host and the native backend by:\n- Registering and unregistering command IDs via the `CommandExecutor` trait in `Service.environment`.\n- Marshaling protobuf `argument` oneofs (String, Int, Bool, Bytes) into `serde_json::Value` for flexible argument passing to the executor.\n- Executing commands asynchronously and returning results or structured errors (`RpcError`) as JSON bytes.\n- Adding detailed logging for command lifecycle events to aid debugging in the extension host environment.\n\nThis completes the bridge for user-initiated actions and extension commands, enabling extensions to register custom commands that trigger native logic or invoke other VS Code commands.",
			"SHA": "d53f35344835e6f664c0d88c40bdecda13954401"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:33:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1068,
				44
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement language feature provider registration and execution handlers\n\nIntroduce the complete set of RPC handlers in `CocoonService` for the `Vine` protocol to bridge the extension host with the Mountain backend. This adds two categories of functionality: provider registration (e.g., `RegisterCompletionItemProvider`, `RegisterDefinitionProvider`) and provider execution (e.g., `ProvideCompletionItems`, `ProvideDefinition`).\n\nThe implementation forwards requests from the gRPC layer to the `LanguageFeatureProviderRegistry` via the `Service.environment` trait methods. Key modifications include:\n- Deserializing URI, range, and position data into `CommonLibrary` DTOs (e.g., `PositionDTO`, `RangeDTO`).\n- Mapping results from the internal registry back into gRPC `Response` shapes (e.g., mapping `Location` structs for `ProvideReferences` and `ProvideDefinition`).\n- Implementing specific logic for `ProvideHover` to join content pieces with Markdown separators.\n- Adding logging for provider lifecycle events and error handling via Tonic `Status`.\n\nThese handlers fulfill the contract for standard VS Code language services, enabling features like go-to-definition, autocomplete, hover info, code actions, and semantic highlighting within the extension host environment.",
			"SHA": "eeb94c2ea005a579d74f0c2b6e47db19abcaa81d"
		},
		{
